WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.260
Right now, the air molecules around you
are moving faster than a jet airliner.

2
00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:09.240
Each one carries its own random
kinetic energy as it moves.

3
00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:11.810
Some molecules are light, some heavy.

4
00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:16.090
Some gases are squeezed into
tanks, some spread through a room.

5
00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:21.230
So what sets how much kinetic energy
each molecule has, on average?

6
00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:25.450
In this mission, you'll calculate
the average energy of one particle,

7
00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:28.220
with one of the smallest
constants in physics.

8
00:00:28.270 --> 00:00:31.300
Then you'll convert
between kelvin and Celsius,

9
00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:34.440
and spot the trap in a
temperature below zero.

10
00:00:34.490 --> 00:00:38.840
Your mission: find out what sets the
energy of the molecules around you.
